{
  "$comment": [
    "The public-post quality rule the server applies before a post goes public (getPublicPostQualityError in src/lib/marketplace-trust.ts).",
    "The app checks the same rule before step 2 says Ready to publish, so it cannot promise a post the server will refuse.",
    "Both read the words rule from one shared module, ugc-mobile/lib/post-publish-policy/post-publish-policy.ts, which lists placeholderTokens and fillerTokens in code; each suite holds its side to these cases: src/__tests__/marketplace-trust.test.ts (server) and ugc-mobile/__tests__/post-new-view-model.test.ts (app).",
    "A title is a placeholder only when every word in it is a placeholder token, a filler token or a number, and at least one is a placeholder token: 'Demo video' is one, 'Product demo' is not. Text with no letters or digits left once links and ASCII punctuation are removed is a placeholder too, and so is keyboard mash ('ababab'); letters of any script count.",
    "A text post (no media) also needs a body of at least minTextLength characters that is not placeholder text. Private posts are not checked."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "placeholderTokens": [
    "asdf",
    "demo",
    "draft",
    "example",
    "foo",
    "ipsum",
    "lorem",
    "placeholder",
    "sample",
    "test",
    "testing",
    "todo",
    "untitled"
  ],
